      "proposed_laureates": ["Francis Halzen", "Albrecht Karle", "Shigeru Yoshida"],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "IceCube established high-energy neutrino astronomy and opened a new observational window on the Universe, a major and lasting advance in astroparticle physics.",
        "attribution": "Halzen was central to the detector’s conception and scientific program; Karle and Yoshida represent major detector and analysis contributions. Credit across a large collaboration remains difficult to divide.",
        "maturity": "The detector and neutrino observations are well established, with astrophysical sources now identified in multiple settings.",
        "uncertainties": ["The relative individual contributions within the collaboration need careful assessment."]
      }
    },
